course: dictionary
lesson: 4116
title: A name, or a bag?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. Context is your clue. «Even in Britain at the time, many people, like the young William Gladstone, called the war shameful.» Here Gladstone is a person's name, because the sentence says «the young William Gladstone».
explain: Gladstone can also be a word for a bag. In old stories a doctor or traveller carries a Gladstone bag. If the sentence talks about a person doing something, the word is a name. If it talks about carrying or packing, the word is probably a bag.
explain: Ask yourself: does this word fit as a person, a thing, or a place? Then test your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Gladstone is a name: William Ewart Gladstone was a British Prime Minister four times in the 1800s.
fact: A Gladstone bag is an old-fashioned leather travelling bag.
fact: A Gladstone bag opens wide into two halves, like a doctor's bag.
fact: Gladstone is also a place name, for example a city in Queensland, Australia.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word is the right one.
exercise: «Even in Britain at the time, many people, like the young William Gladstone, called the war shameful.» Who is Gladstone in this sentence? | *A person, William Ewart Gladstone, who later became a British Prime Minister | A bag made of leather | A kind of old castle | A city in Australia
exercise: In old stories a doctor carries a Gladstone bag. What is a Gladstone bag? | A glass jar for medicine | *An old-fashioned leather travelling bag that opens wide into two halves | A modern rucksack with wheels | A tiny purse for coins
exercise: Gladstone is also a place name. Which place is it? | A bus route in London | A famous castle in Wales | A river in Canada | *A city in Queensland, Australia
test: Which meaning of Gladstone fits this sentence: «She packed her shirts and socks into the old Gladstone and snapped it shut.»? | A person's name | A city in Australia | *A leather travelling bag that opens into two halves
test: Read this: «The Prime Minister, Gladstone, spoke to the Queen about the new law.» What is Gladstone in this sentence? | *A person's name | A leather bag | A place in Queensland
exam: Which two words in «Even in Britain at the time, many people, like the young William Gladstone, called the war shameful.» tell you Gladstone is a person? | Britain and war | many and people | *William and young | called and shameful
